Fri Nov 13 20:10:00 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add ted-2.23-motif-xft-ruler-text.patch: with an Xft render
  table the Motif rulers and the "Page n/n, Section n/n" status
  line were drawn with a core bitmap font (jagged, no
  antialiasing); keep the render table's Xft font in the ruler's
  screen font as well, so Ted's Xft text path draws them
  antialiased like the rest of the GUI

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 19:30:00 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add ted-2.23-motif-format-tool-size.patch: with an Xft render
  table Motif sizes an XmText as XmNcolumns times the font's
  max_advance_width (16px for Droid Sans 10, twice a digit), and
  since Ted's rows split into equal columns the Format Tool opened
  606px wide instead of 360px; size the text boxes by the width
  of an average digit instead. Also let the user resize the
  Format Tool (the minimum stays the size that fits every page),
  as Ted-gtk already does

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 17:40:00 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add ted-2.23-gtk-ibeam-cursor.patch: Ted-gtk created the I-beam
  document cursor but never put it on the text area, so the pointer
  stayed an arrow over the document; set it on the drawing area
  when it is realized, as the Motif version does with XDefineCursor
  (the rulers keep the arrow)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 16:40:20 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add a Brazilian Portuguese spelling dictionary (pt_BR.dfa) to
  ted-spell: upstream ted_pt_BR.tar.gz is a UI translation only.
  ted-pt_BR-wordlist.py (Source3) derives ~763k clean inflected
  forms from VERO (myspell-pt_BR) with a morphological-family
  heuristic instead of a full unmunch (10.5M forms with hyphenated
  enclisis, truncated verb forms, pre-AO90 spellings and rare 1913
  stems), and ted-mkdfa.c (Source4) compiles the list with Ted's
  own lib/ind.a into a minimised automaton (~4.9 MB)
- Name the pt_BR and pt_PT dictionaries in Ted-pt_BR.properties
  (Ted.NAME_pt_BR / Ted.NAME_pt_PT)
- BuildRequires: myspell-pt_BR, python3-base

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 12:48:11 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add ted-2.23-motif-center-on-pointer-monitor.patch: the Motif
  VendorShell always sets a program-specified position of 0,0, so
  every Motif window (documents, main window, tools) opened in the
  top left corner of the whole desktop; on first show, center it on
  the Xinerama/RandR monitor that holds the pointer, as the GTK
  version does with GTK_WIN_POS_CENTER (a *geometry resource still
  wins)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 05:00:53 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Do not apply the upstream ted.gtkrc-2.0 compact styles: zeroed
  x/ythickness and 8px option menu indicators made the GTK Format
  Tool look cramped under most themes (clipped borders, arrow
  offset, entries indistinguishable from the background); the
  original is installed as ted.gtkrc-2.0.upstream

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 04:53:16 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add ted-2.23-motif-selection-format32.patch: on 64-bit the Motif
  version answered TARGETS selection requests (e.g. from a
  clipboard manager such as CopyQ) with property format
  8*sizeof(Atom) = 64, and the resulting X BadValue error made Ted
  exit as soon as text was selected (e.g. clicking a link in the
  help document); use format 32 and type ATOM, and format 32 for
  copied pixmaps

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 04:36:40 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add ted-2.23-motif-xft-default-font.patch: the Motif version
  crashed at startup when the widget font came from an Xft
  renderTable (e.g. "*renderTable" with fontType FONT_IS_XFT, as
  set by CDE/NsCDE), because the XftFont was used as an XFontSet;
  load a core font of the same pixel size instead
- Add ted-2.23-gtk-default-font-size.patch: the GTK version only
  honoured absolute theme font sizes (and without dividing by
  PANGO_SCALE), so text drawn with the default font fell back to
  10 pixels; convert point sizes using the screen resolution
- Stop ted.gtkrc-2.0 from forcing "Sans 7" on the Format Tool and
  on every option menu (also squeezed the print dialog)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 04:09:18 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Initial package of Ted 2.23 (last upstream release, 2013)
  * Ted is built twice: Motif (/usr/bin/Ted, main package) and
    GTK+ 2 (/usr/bin/Ted-gtk, ted-gtk subpackage); data files are
    shared in ted-common
  * Add ted-2.23-memory-bugs.patch, fixing problems reported by
    GCC 15 and not addressed by any distribution:
    + bmpng.c: heap overflow writing palette[256] when saving a
      paletted PNG with alpha
    + utilDosTime.c: uninitialized time_t used for ZIP (EPUB)
      timestamps
    + drawMetafileSvg.c: SVG pattern viewBox used the width twice
  * Ship the upstream localization tarballs split into ted-spell
    (dictionaries) and ted-lang (UI translations, selected from
    the locale, and localized manuals), without Supplements
  * Install rtf2pdf, rtf2ps, rtf2html, rtf2txt and rtf2epub in
    /usr/bin and the man pages with the data directory filled in
  * Own desktop entries and icon name
